# GY-87 Sensor Test

This example demonstrates how to initialize and read the sensors integrated into the GY-87 module using the ESP32 and the ESP-IDF framework.

## Sensors

The tested module contains two I²C devices:

| Sensor | Function | I²C Address |
|---|---|---|
| MPU6050 | 3-axis accelerometer and 3-axis gyroscope | `0x68` |
| QMC5883L | 3-axis magnetometer | `0x0D` |

**Note:** This hardware configuration uses the QMC5883L magnetometer instead of the HMC5883L.

## Hardware Connections

| GY-87 Pin | ESP32 Pin |
|---|---|
| VCC | 3.3V |
| GND | GND |
| SDA | GPIO 21 |
| SCL | GPIO 22 |

The module is connected directly to the ESP32 I²C bus. No TCA9548A multiplexer is required when using a single GY-87 module.

## Test Features

The example performs the following operations:

1. Initializes the I²C bus.
2. Initializes the MPU6050.
3. Enables I²C bypass to access the magnetometer.
4. Initializes the QMC5883L.
5. Reads accelerometer, gyroscope, and magnetometer measurements.
6. Prints the measurements to the serial monitor.

## Serial Output

The example periodically displays:

| Measurement | Unit |
|---|---|
| Accelerometer X, Y, Z | g |
| Gyroscope X, Y, Z | °/s |
| Magnetometer X, Y, Z | Raw values |

The accelerometer should measure approximately 1 g along the axis aligned with gravity when the module is stationary.

Gyroscope readings should remain close to zero when the module is not rotating.

Magnetometer readings depend on the module's orientation and surrounding magnetic environment.

## Notes

- The magnetometer measurements are raw and have not been calibrated.
- Magnetic interference from nearby electronic components may affect the readings.
- The example uses the GY-87 driver implemented in `src/components/gy87.cpp` and `src/components/gy87.h`.